{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>הוות</b> — occurrences are called הוות, that is, the foolish son brings הוות upon his father." "<b>דלף</b> — that is, a dripping [that] harasses one's affairs drives people away; so the contentions of a wife, like troubles." "Another interpretation: <b>דלף טורד</b> — that does not cease. And after he spoke of the fool and the evil wife, he said: for a house and wealth fathers bequeath to their children, but they cannot bequeath to them the wife who has acquired wisdom, for it is from HaShem."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:40.496595354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}